2026-11-06T21:50Z LIMIT FOUND. The cloud environment's network policy is "limited" with no allowed hosts: curl and WebFetch to almost every source host (rand.org, arxiv.org, nber.org, bls.gov, census.gov, gartner.com, mckinsey.com, pewresearch.org, ftc.gov, sec.gov, etc.) are refused by the egress proxy. Only WebSearch works, and it has a cap of about 200 searches per turn shared across all agents. Consequence: findings rest on search-engine extracts that cite primary URLs, not on full reads; verbatim quotes cannot be verified against fetched pages. Did NOT request a network change because that needs the user's live approval and the user is asleep. Decision: continue search-only, label every finding's basis, run gap-filling passes in later turns.
